Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","key":"dnsv6VSg58"},{"type":"text","value":" falls outside the confidence interval, reject H~o~.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"GBGz7B8i12"}],"key":"DkYPEblRBm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"knwdgRBqhy"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"\\mu_{0}","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","key":"t11KYtMaIH"},{"type":"text","value":" falls inside the confidence interval, do not reject H~o~.","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"CCmB0pTXCH"}],"key":"YzuRXBn2R6"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"R31fdhYE33"}],"key":"rCLqy35Kdw"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"We'll use example 2, in which the alternative was two-sided.\n\nRecall that we want to check whether a medication conforms to a target concentration of a chemical ingredient by testing\n\n$H_{0}:\\mu=250$\n\n$H_{a}:\\mu\\neq250$\n\nWe assume that $\\sigma=12$, and in a sample of size n = 100 we obtained a sample mean of $\\bar{x}=247$.\n\nA 95% confidence interval for μ is $\\bar{x}\\pm2\\frac{\\sigma}{\\sqrt{n}}=247\\pm2\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{100}}=247\\pm2.4=\\left(244.6, 249.4\\right)$.\n\nSince the interval does not contain 250, we reject H~o~ and conclude that the alternative is true: the population mean concentration differs from 250.\n\n```{figure} images/image354.gif\n:alt: A number line showing the 95% confidence interval, which is (244.6, 249.4). 250 is also marked on the number line, and it isn&apos;t within the interval, so we can be confident that μ isn&apos;t 250. In other words, we can reject the hypothesis H_0:μ = 250\n```","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"bq1U3FAB5M"}],"key":"ks36DkMoyl"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Did I Get This?","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"UVKNkg0sem"}],"identifier":"did-i-get-this","label":"Did I Get This?","html_id":"did-i-get-this","implicit":true,"key":"q88Ki5Dcc6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the following is an actual Minitab output; the others were edited to be incorrect.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"afSIyYwWWx"}],"key":"p0WtznUwzN"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/image392-240ebb733240662575434aa6ad8a7353.gif","alt":"Output: One-Sample Z: Test of mu=264 vs not = 264 The assumed standard deviation = 16 N: 35 Mean: 260.000 SE Mean: 2.704 95% CI: (254.699, 265.301) Z: -2.22 P: 0.047","key":"Z2iBqsc1np","urlSource":"images/image392.gif"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"nC4yaC2fTx"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/image393-796076f1c9f057c6110f9a531234cd75.gif","alt":"Output: One-Sample Z: Test of mu=267 vs not = 267 The assumed standard deviation = 16 N: 35 Mean: 260.000 SE Mean: 2.704 95% CI: (254.699, 265.301) Z: -2.22 P: 0.087","key":"wEpKT1fhSJ","urlSource":"images/image393.gif"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"vU8Z8hxyoV"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/image394-6d65e20a84ea66ae4b31b8e6440892b1.gif","alt":"Output: One-Sample Z: Test of mu=266 vs not = 266 The assumed standard deviation = 16 N: 35 Mean: 260.000 SE Mean: 2.704 95% CI: (254.699, 265.301) Z: -2.22 P: 0.027","key":"QdoKoa7sjx","urlSource":"images/image394.gif"}],"enumerator":"3","key":"Pz3sAYhGRd"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"PV1YP15bFu"}],"key":"gnoQAmLMWS"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"**Sectionnest**\n\n*(Interactive activity — available in the OLI platform)*","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"BRMCdZ89mO"}],"key":"UA0tWEO5jN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Did You Get It?","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"wrP1AIpeRH"}],"key":"KfzExuMqpo"},{"type":"text","value":" If so, then go ahead and move on. If not, then click the link below for some additional practice.","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"YqJMwDScxF"}],"key":"kGMRjeL4yW"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"VpR72AiZOp"}],"key":"exyA3kEfyB"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"**Sectionnest**\n\nHypothesis Testing for the Population Mean (Extra Problem)\n\n*(Interactive activity — available in the OLI platform)*","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"jCP5PV9xD2"}],"key":"Of8TRC5CQg"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comment","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"AikQTwhNAr"}],"identifier":"comment","label":"Comment","html_id":"comment","implicit":true,"key":"rWpcun3QvN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Beyond using the confidence interval as a quick way to carry out the two-sided test, the confidence interval can provide insight into the actual value of the population mean if H~o~ is rejected. In the concentration level example, H~o~ was rejected, and all we could conclude about the mean concentration level of the entire shipment, μ, was that it was not 250. The 95% confidence interval for μ (244.6, 249.4) gives us an idea of what plausible values for μ would be. In particular, we can conclude that since the confidence interval lies below 250, at least a large portion of the shipment contains medication that is ineffective.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"Ke2vXMHo2t"}],"key":"uBxsRNoOrb"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"r1zjFDYqSs"}],"key":"Ocfaard9aW"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"**Learn By Doing**\n\nHypothesis Testing for the Population Mean\n\n*(Interactive activity — available in the OLI platform)*","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"iuEYzTu32n"}],"key":"Khe9RoKUws"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do you feel that you understand this concept?","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"qZY0g3LrSu"}],"key":"vy8oxBovsT"},{"type":"text","value":" If so, then go ahead and move on. If not, then click the link below for some additional practice.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"hbanjF2sV6"}],"key":"CbrV3qf1fe"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"QskMlbS1i3"}],"key":"o0XFfc9wAm"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"**Learn By Doing**\n\nHypothesis Testing for the Population Mean (Extra Problems)\n\n*(Interactive activity — available in the OLI platform)*","position":{"start":{"line"